Implementation

Part 1 provides 16 per-process descriptors, initially including stdin
and stdout, and implements creat/open/read/write/close/unlink using the
stub filesystem and virtual-memory copies.

Part 2 maintains a locked global free-page list. loadSections allocates
individual physical pages and installs per-process translations, including
read-only COFF pages. unloadSections returns those pages. Virtual-memory
copies translate each page and stop on invalid or read-only destinations.

Part 3 implements exec, join and exit with unique process IDs and
per-process child tables. exec validates arguments and loads a new child;
join uses KThread.join and returns a direct child's exit status once.
Normal and abnormal exits close files and free memory. Interrupt-protected
counters track process IDs and live processes. Only the root process can
call halt, and the last exiting process terminates the kernel. Invalid
syscall arguments return -1.

Validation performed on November 7, 2026 (America/Los_Angeles)

Java: clean build with Eclipse Temurin Java 21 on macOS.
C: the official Fall 2026 MIPS cross-compiler in a temporary Ubuntu 22.04
container, with qemu-i386 for its legacy x86 binaries. The resulting COFF
programs were executed by the local Nachos simulator.

All 24 program/seed/memory configurations passed:
- Official exit1, except1, exec1, join1 and execarg1 examples.
- Root halt.coff.
- p3_test: 668 checks each with seeds 1, 2, 3, 7, 42 and 99. Covers argument
  contents and limits, cross-page filename/argv/status copies, null/invalid
  pointers, argument-page overflow, negative exit status, parent-only join,
  duplicate join, exceptions, code-page write protection, child halt,
  private descriptors, monotonic PIDs and repeated process creation.
  A gated child verifies that invalid join status returns before waiting.
- p3_lowmem: 40 rounds each at 20, 32 and 64 physical pages. These allow
  0, 1 and 3 blocked children respectively. Each round also attempts 40
  failed execs at capacity, then joins children and reuses the freed pages.
- p3_orphan: seeds 1, 7 and 42. The parent exits first, and its child
  continues, fails to halt as an orphan, and exits last.
- Existing write_basic, create_basic, read_basic, fd_limits and io_pages.
- sh.coff: echo hello, cat exit1.c, and exit.

A diagnostic autograder outside the submitted source tree recorded actual
exit statuses and inspected final resource counts. Every exit-based run
ended with zero live processes, all physical pages free and zero stub
filesystem handles. Root halt is intentionally an immediate machine stop.
The negative-status test handles the sign itself because the supplied
test-library atoi does not recognize '-'. No library code was changed.

To reproduce on ieng6 after prepping the course environment:
  cd nachos/proj2
  make test
  make
  nachos -x join1.coff
  nachos -s 1 -x p3_test.coff
  nachos -m 20 -x p3_lowmem.coff
  nachos -m 32 -x p3_lowmem.coff
  nachos -m 64 -x p3_lowmem.coff
  nachos -x p3_orphan.coff
  nachos -x sh.coff

The final code has not been run on ieng6 or submitted to Gradescope during
this session. Local test success is not a claim about hidden-grader results.

